      "reasoning": "The combat went well. I traded `Muxus` for both `Sabertooth Mauler` and `Elvish Archdruid`. That's a 2-for-1 trade in my favor, removing their scaling threat and their mana lord.\n\
Now the board is:\n\
Me:\n\
- Beetleback Chief (2/2)\n\
- 2x Goblin Tokens (1/1)\n\
- Blisterpod (1/1)\n\
- Hand: `Brood Monitor`, `Ornery Goblin`\n\
- Lands: 6 (5 tapped, Ash Barrens untapped, Mountains/Thriving Bluff/Forest available) — Wait, last priority pass said untapping happened. It's my precombat main. I have 6 lands available.\n\
\n\
Opponent:\n\
- Keeper of Fables (4/5) (sick)\n\
- 6 lands (5 tapped)\n\
- Hand: 2 cards\n\
\n\
Threat assessment: `Keeper of Fables` is a 4/5 value engine. My current board is all small creatures (2/2s and 1/1s). I can't attack profitably into the 4/5 right now.\n\
\n\
My options:\n\
1.  **Cast Brood Monitor ({4}{G}{G})**:\n\
    - Creates a 3/3 and three 1/1 Scions.\n\
    - Adds 4 bodies to the board.\n\
    - Total power added: 6.\n\
    - Stalls the ground against Keeper of Fables.\n\
    - Leaves me with a wide board to go around the Keeper next turn or chump it forever.\n\
2.  **Cast Ornery Goblin ({1}{R})**:\n\
    - 2/1 that deals 1 damage when blocked/blocking.\n\
    - Pretty weak here. Doesn't trade with Keeper (4/5 takes 2+1=3 damage).\n\
\n\
The play is clearly `Brood Monitor`. It stabilizes the board, provides sacrificial mana if I draw something big, and widens my board significantly. With the 3 goblins I already have + Blisterpod + Monitor + 3 Scions, I'll have 8 creatures. The opponent has 1. I can start attacking wide around the Keeper next turn.\n\
\n\
Sequencing:\n\
- Play Brood Monitor.\n\
- Do I attack?\n\
    - Opponent has a 4/5 Keeper.\n\
    - If I attack with everything (2/2, 1/1, 1/1, 1/1):\n\
        - Keeper blocks Beetleback Chief (2/2). Chief dies. Opponent takes 3 damage.\n\
        - Keeper blocks a 1/1. 1/1 dies. Opponent takes 4 damage.\n\
    - Losing a real creature for 3-4 damage isn't worth it yet. I'll wait until my army is overwhelming or I draw a pump spell/removal.\n\
\n\
Plan: Cast Brood Monitor, pass turn.\n\
\n\
